<ContentLayout section="legal" title="Privacy policy" heading="Privacy policy" updated="5 October 2026">
  <p><strong>Draft for legal review.</strong> This covers UK GDPR and US state privacy laws such as the CCPA (plan 09).</p>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>CharFlut ("we") sells print-on-demand clothing at charflut.com. Contact: privacy@charflut.com.</p>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Orders:</strong> name, email, phone, delivery address, items bought, payment status (never your card number).</li>
    <li><strong>Account:</strong> email address and saved addresses, if you create an account.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> email address and when you joined, if you sign up.</li>
    <li><strong>Site use:</strong> anonymous, cookie-free statistics from Cloudflare Web Analytics.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Print partners (Printify, Printful) to print and ship your order.</li>
    <li>WebXPay (and PayPal, when available) to take payment.</li>
    <li>Our email provider to send receipts and updates.</li>
    <li>Cloudflare, which hosts the site and database.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We never sell your personal data.</p>
  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Order records are kept for 7 years for tax purposes. Newsletter data is kept until you unsubscribe.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to marketing at any time. Email privacy@charflut.com. UK residents can complain to the ICO; California residents have rights under the CCPA, including the right to know and to delete.</p>
</ContentLayout>
